ces from 74% to 51% (+0.15).","26.Bf5 opens the line of the queen on g2 to the g7 pawn.","Black answers 26…Nd4, attacking the bishop on f5, which is undefended.","After 26…Nd4 27.Bb1 Ne6 28.Qh3 Nxf4 29.Nd7, White is a pawn down (+2.32)."]},{"ply":52,"name":"26…Ne7","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"26…Ne7 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 30% to 18%.","points":["White answers 27.Bc2, which moves the attacked bishop to safety.","After Bc2, White wins 1 point of material within 6 moves.","Better was 26…Nd4 (+2.32), which attacks the bishop on f5, which is undefended."],"better":"26…Nd4 threatens …Nxf5, winning a bishop, and stops Rg3. After 27.Bb1 Ne6 28.Qh3 Nxf4 29.Nd7 N6h5, Black comes out a pawn up (+2.32)."},{"ply":59,"name":"30.Nh4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"30.Nh4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moving away uncovers the queen on g2, which now hits the g7 pawn.","The next best move, 30.Ne5, would drop White's winning chances from 92% to 60% (+1.14).","30.Nh4 threatens Qxg7#, with mate in 1, and stops …Rxe3.","It threatens Qxg7#, with mate in 1, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black was threatening …Rxe3, winning a rook. Nh4 takes care of it.","Black answers 30…Re7."]},{"ply":61,"name":"31.Rg3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"31.Rg3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook takes the half-open g-file, aiming at the g7 pawn.","Moves the attacked rook to safety.","The next best move, 31.Ng6, would drop White's winning chances from 93% to 82% (+4.03).","31.Rg3 threatens Rxg7+, with mate in 4, and gets the rook out of the way of …Rxe3.","It threatens Rxg7+, with mate in 4, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black was threatening …Rxe3, winning a rook. The rook steps away."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined: Exchange Variation, Positional Variation","eco":"D35","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 14…Bf